course: dictionary
lesson: 423
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning the writer means. Read the whole sentence, then ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «Put on your apron before you start painting.» Here an apron is a piece of cloth you tie over your clothes to keep them clean. Now read a different sentence: «At the airport, the planes were loaded on the apron.» The clue is airport, so this apron is the area where planes park.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the cloth meaning still makes sense, you have it. If not, try the next meaning. The clues in the sentence decide which one is right.
fact: An apron is a piece of cloth you tie over the front of your clothes to keep them clean.
fact: At an airport, the apron is the area where planes park and are loaded.
fact: The apron of a stage is the part in front of the curtain.
fact: «An old shirt or apron protects your clothes from paint, which stains.»
fact: Chefs, bakers and blacksmiths wear aprons, and children often wear them for cooking, baking, painting and science experiments.
exercise: «Paint stains clothes, so you wear an old shirt or apron.» What is an apron in this sentence? | A kind of paint | *A piece of cloth you tie over your clothes | The area where planes park | The part of a stage in front of the curtain
exercise: At the airport, the planes were loaded on the apron. What does apron mean here? | A cloth tied over your clothes | The front part of a stage | *The area where planes park and are loaded | A kind of plane
exercise: Which phrase is one you might hear in a cooking lesson? | Park an apron | Paint the stage apron | *Put on an apron | Load the apron onto a plane
test: «Acrylic becomes plastic when dry and does not wash out easily, so artists wear old clothes or aprons.» What does apron mean here? | The part of a stage in front of the curtain | The area at an airport where planes park | *A cloth you tie over your clothes to keep them clean | A bonnet worn by painters
test: «For his money Toad gets a cotton print gown, an apron, a shawl, and a rusty black bonnet.» Which of these is the apron? | A stage in front of a curtain | A shawl for a cold night | A rusty black bonnet | *A cloth worn over the front of the clothes
exam: «The apron of the stage was lit by a single light.» Which meaning of apron fits? | A cloth worn to keep clothes clean | A piece of paint | The area where planes park | *The part of the stage in front of the curtain
